jcopelan@nyx10.cs.du.edu (Jim Copeland) writes:

>"Thou shalt be my Envoy of Balance!"  You feel unworthy.

>What does the unworthy part mean??

When you become EoB, various things can happen. You gain a few
intrinsics and your prayer-timeout becomes much higher. Also, you can
gain a good weapon.

To gain this weapon, you must be wielding a long sword (when lawful)
which is changed into Excalibur. If you are chaotic, you don't need to
have  sword already: Stormbringer is just created if it did not exist
already, else, an ordinary broadsword is created.

If you are neutral, like you are, you gain Vorpal Blade, if it did not
exist yet.

Then, regardless of alignment or artifact status, your weapon is
"enhanced": it is made rustproof, and enchanted to at least +1. If this
is in some way impossible to do, THEN "You feel unworthy.".

